{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103274","id":2356251402,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6McYsK","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103274","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103274.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103274.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103274","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103274/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103274/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103274/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e98f715b92642fd49d85d8cb2d1748d3c60fc87f","number":103274,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add custom shader support to SpriteBase3D","user":{"login":"chocola-mint","id":56677134,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2Njc3MTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56677134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint","html_url":"https://github.com/chocola-mint","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chocola-mint/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/3266\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103274#issuecomment-5279657807 for the latest revision of this PR.\r\n\r\n<details><summary><h3>Original version of the PR can be found here<h2></summary>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b1237b71-8053-4bac-bc51-b035df48f8d9\r\n\r\nThis PR lets custom shaders (via Material Override) access the sprite texture used by SpriteBase3D. (and its child classes Sprite3D and AnimatedSprite3D by extension)\r\n\r\nValidation is implemented to warn the user if a Material Override without the necessary uniforms (namely `uniform sampler2D texture_albedo` and `uniform ivec2 albedo_texture_size`) is being used. The \"Flags\" group properties of SpriteBase3D are also hidden when a Material Override is being used, as those properties are used in the default automatic material generation. (`StandardMaterial3D::get_material_for_2d()`) The user can reimplement those features in the custom shader code anyway, so they have been hidden.\r\n\r\nSide note: This pattern of requiring the shader to have uniforms of specific names and types can be turned into a reusable \"shader interface/trait\" system if needed. Users could make their own high-level 3D nodes that send data to shaders like SpriteBase3D does. (Maybe a more advanced version of Sprite3D that assigns normal maps and SDF texture maps as uniforms) The main benefit of such a system would be to reduce the amount of builtin shader types, though. (No need to add a new `sprite_3d` shader type) Though this probably would have to be a separate proposal.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThis PR was originally made to add custom shader support for AnimatedSprite3D in particular, but it is evident that implementing the support for SpriteBase3D makes more sense here.\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n</details> ","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"